#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Stock Market Participants]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Buyers 💰]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[  - Purchase stocks]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Sellers 📉]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[  - Sell their stocks]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("The stock market functions through the activities of two main types of participants: buyers and sellers.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Buyers are investors who purchase stocks, essentially buying ownership in a company.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("On the other hand, sellers are investors who sell their stocks, relinquishing their ownership in a company.")
]
#only("4")[
#voiceover("The interaction between buyers and sellers is what drives the stock market.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Buyer and Seller Motivations]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Buyers: Potential for profit 📈]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[  - Believe stock price will increase]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Sellers: Realize gains or limit losses 💸]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[  - Believe stock price will decrease or need cash]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Buyers are motivated by the potential for profit. They purchase stocks because they believe the stock price will increase in the future, allowing them to sell at a higher price and make a profit.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For example, if a buyer purchases a stock at $100 and the price increases to $150, they can sell the stock and make a $50 profit per share.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Sellers, on the other hand, are motivated by the desire to realize gains or limit losses. They sell stocks because they believe the stock price will decrease in the future, or because they need the cash for other purposes.")
]
#only("4")[
#voiceover("For instance, if a seller bought a stock at $50 and the price has increased to $100, they may choose to sell to lock in their $50 per share profit.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Market Dynamics]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Supply and demand 🔄]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[  - Buyer demand increases prices 📈]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[  - Seller supply decreases prices 📉]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[- Equilibrium: Balanced supply and demand]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("The interaction between buyers and sellers creates the market dynamics of supply and demand.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("When there are more buyers than sellers, the demand for the stock increases, driving the price up.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Conversely, when there are more sellers than buyers, the supply of the stock increases, pushing the price down.")
]
#only("4")[
#voiceover("The market reaches equilibrium when the supply and demand are balanced, resulting in a stable stock price.")
]
]

